## TokenLighten MCP

TokenLighten (TL) returns exact slices + edit handles cheaply. When TL is exposed, Start EVERY file task with it before Read/Grep/cat: Code/docs/config/logs/Office/archives=>`read_file mode=task_pack query="<verbatim request>"`+known `paths`; never truncate/summarize. If the host reports native-bypass or exposes no TL, use native; never activate TL mid-task. `taskProfile`: user-declared `answer`=read-only,`generic`=change; never infer task-specific hints; change-task sub-questions stay `generic`/omitted. Shared workspace: every agent passes its fixed `lane`; omit when alone. Worktree: pass your own `cwd` on EVERY call; otherwise `cwd-required-for-edit`. STANDING RULE: a different task re-packs with `taskEpoch:"new"`.

Pasted/attached docs need no reread; TL=workspace-only; use `did_you_mean`/`cwd_candidates`.

- Every reply is `{v:1,kind,...}`; `kind` alone says what you got — branch on it, not on a field's presence; absence is meaning (no `limit`=complete). The 15: `read.task_pack|text|map|batch|artifact|receipt|closure`, `search.matches|references|tree`, `edit.applied|reclassified|rolled_back|state_unknown`, `refusal`. An unrecognized `kind`=SAFE-STOP: report it, issue no edit, never infer from fields.
- Act on `decision.kind` (`read.task_pack`): `act.answer`/`act.edit`=>discovery closed; answer/edit NOW from served content, batch every ready independent concern — including independent regression-test additions — in exactly ONE `edit_file` `edits[]` call; once `prepared`, do not read/search again. `act.edit` carries the writable `frontier`, sometimes a ready `apply`. `discover`=>run its `next` (each, if several); a `gaps` `code` is SEMANTIC — no call rides it and more bytes never close one. `await_input`=>use served `candidates` bodies when safe, else ask. `done`=>stop. Everything else on a pack rides `plan`, starting with `evidence_model`.
- `refusal`: `code` says what failed, `retry` is the ONLY sanctioned transition. `call`=fix the named `field` (path-qualified; `did_you_mean`=near-miss, `keys`=what IS advertised) and re-issue. `challenge`=re-issue the same call with a `challenge` you author from its advertised request schema, only when new evidence changes the certified decision. `user-input`=ask. `new-task`=re-pack. `none`=this call shape is closed; `remaining`=owed work. `detail`/`candidate`/`expected_shapes`/`nearest_match` are ADVISORY — recover from them, never branch on them; on `nearest_match.out_of_range` re-issue against a covering handle, no re-read. `cause:"capped"` means truncated bytes; follow `next` (smaller scope/request), then retry. Every `next` is executable: run it verbatim, never as a template.
- `read.receipt`=your context is already current, by tag: `pack-unchanged`; `code-unchanged` (`served_by` names the earlier call that put the bytes on the wire — provenance, not a new read); `decision-unchanged` (the certified DECISION stands, not the bytes; `certified_query`=what it closed); `kit-unchanged`; `closure-complete`. Never dead-end on a receipt: follow its `next`, or act on the evidence it restates.
- Zoom: `evidence` items carry `body`=served now, `prior`=already in context (skip), `remaining`=unserved windows of that handle (`ranges=[..]` for several), `role`=surface. `limit`=response-level truncation; a recoverable `cause` (`wire`/`records`) ALWAYS carries `next` — run it, `source` never has one. `read.map`/`search.tree` have no range to zoom — re-request the named `symbol`/`path`; `read.artifact` addresses by `sheet`/`slides`/`pages`/`rows`/`sections`; `read.batch` entries carry their own `truncated`. `mode=full` past the per-task cap returns skeleton+`remaining_ranges`+a `next` — take the slice, don't retry full. Re-pack with the returned `qref`, no `query`.
- Search: `action=find query=<one identifier>`; inventory=>`tree`; call sites=>`references`; 0-match+`absence`=that token verifiably absent, no re-grep; `references` pages via `limit`: run the returned `next` to exhaustion for full recall via `files`, never hand-build its `cursor`; `coverage_reason=candidate-list`=>run the `decision` `next` (qref+paths), never a serial `mode=full` sweep; same-task restatement auto-binds candidates.
- Edit: prepared `fast_path.kind="single-site-unique-match"` proves one edit, not an applied edit: call `edit_file` once with its `handle`/`search`/`replace`/`precondition`+`allowPathFallback:false`; no re-read/re-pack. Otherwise edit read handles, batch `edits[]`, use `unique-match`/item. A ready `change_contract` is the bounded effect area: edit only `action:"edit"` obligations by dependency stage, batch independent items; `action:"review"` is evidence, not an automatic write. New files/scratch/tests=>`create:true` with explicit `cwd` (or rooted handle); on `cwd-required-for-create`, choose from served `cwd_candidates` and resend — never native Write/Edit in-workspace; >32 KiB=fail. `edit.applied`=it landed: `core` (`counts`+`paths`)=post-edit truth, `applied`+`brace_delta`=per-file detail, `reclassification`=the answer->edit fence. `edit.rolled_back`=nothing stands; `edit.state_unknown`=disk unproven, run its `recovery` first.
- Wiring packs (`plan` `wiring`)=>write only `edit_frontier`; `mode=construct-receiver`=>follow its `next`; artifact packs need content-bearing `artifact_sections` per source.
- Archives: read via `read_file mode=archive|task_pack archive={path,member?}` + `search_files find|tree`; virtual member handles stay immutable; no native extraction. With `--allow-write` edit the outer ZIP only via `edit_file artifact={kind:"zip",members:[...]}`; tar/tar.gz/7z/rar remain read-only.
- Credentials: opaque `credentialRef`/`outputCredentialRef` only, never passwords; refs resolve from server `TOKENLIGHTEN_PASSWORD_<REF>`.
- Shell: build/tests/git only — never replace a TL-readable read with `cat`/`sed`/`rg`/native Read.
- `verifying`: after edits run tests or `diff`; a `verification` kit (tests/mocks referencing your edits, with handles) rides the edit/closure response — build harnesses from those handles (new files via `create:true`), never native reads/writes; kit bodies: `code`=served here, `served-earlier`=already in context (skip), `omitted`=NOT served (not empty)=>one batched `handles` read via its `next` — run it before your first compile/test command; `named_paths`/`missing_include_handles`=a path+handle pair, same call; `kit-unchanged`=nothing new. If a successful edit leaves `read.closure` open, use that closure or `next`; otherwise a passing relevant test or diff ends the task — do not call `mode=closure` ceremonially. Never retry a failed edit verbatim; once tests pass, stop — no cosmetic/whitespace polish edits.

